---
description: Use the managed local Graphify graph for structural code questions when it exists.
alwaysApply: true
---

For structural codebase questions, consult an existing
`${PLUGIN_DATA}/graphify-out/graph.json` through the `graphify` skill or the
`graphify` MCP server (`graphify-mcp` from a host-installed `graphifyy[mcp]`).
Use query/path/explain results to locate relevant source; verify current code
and keep inferred relationships distinct from extracted edges. An absent or
stale graph is missing context, not permission to invent relationships or
automatically rebuild it.

The host installs `graphifyy[mcp]`. The MCP server reads
`${PLUGIN_DATA}/graphify-out/graph.json`. Provider/model calls, semantic media
extraction, watching, publication, and delegation retain the current task's
explicit scope. Code-only extraction is available without model credentials.
Keep session evidence under `.tkstack/sessions/<session>/`. Current
instructions retain precedence.
